 See Śukra, I. 120.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["साहसाधिपतिः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["sAhasADipatiH"]}], "sahasamalaNka": [{"id": "sAhasamallANka", "headword": "साहसमल्लाङ्क", "headword_slp1": "sAhasamallANka", "fold": "sahasamalaNka", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "sāhasamallāṅka (BL), epithet of a year of the Kalacuri era probably through confusion, as normally the expression would mean the Vikrama era.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "sahasransu": [{"id": "sahasrAMSu", "headword": "सहस्रांशु", "headword_slp1": "sahasrAMSu", "fold": "sahasransu", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "sahasr-āṃśu (IE 7-1-2), ‘twelve’.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["सहस्रांशुः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["sahasrAMSuH"]}], "sahasrayatana": [{"id": "sahasrAyatana", "headword": "सहस्रायतन", "headword_slp1": "sahasrAyatana", "fold": "sahasrayatana", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "sahasr-āyatana (EI 29), epithet of a temple; literally, ‘having one thousand rooms or shrines’.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "sahi": [{"id": "sAhi", "headword": "साहि", "headword_slp1": "sAhi", "fold": "sahi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "Sāhi, Śāhī (IE 8-2; EI 30; LL), same as Persian Shāh, Old Persian Kshāyathiya; royal title used by some Indian rulers of foreign origin.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "sahijada": [{"id": "sAhijAdA", "headword": "साहिजादा", "headword_slp1": "sAhijAdA", "fold": "sahijada", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "Sāhijādā (BL), title of a prince; same as Persian Shāhzādah. See Sāhiyādā.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "sahikari": [{"id": "sahIkarI", "headword": "सहीकरी", "headword_slp1": "sahIkarI", "fold": "sahikari", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "